WEBVTT

00:05.220 --> 00:10.210
<b>Starting Town
Firstia</b>

00:07.530 --> 00:09.060
Awesome...

00:09.060 --> 00:12.150
That's gotta be high-level
equipment... right?

00:12.480 --> 00:14.220
And that crest...

00:14.220 --> 00:16.240
It's from that achievement-focused
clan, right?

00:17.030 --> 00:20.240
What's someone like that doing
here in the starting town?

00:17.030 --> 00:21.740
The Rampant Forest

00:21.740 --> 00:22.760
<b><i>Sugar</i></b>

00:21.740 --> 00:23.180
<b><i>Kit</i></b>

00:21.740 --> 00:23.260
<b><i>Orga</i></b>

00:21.740 --> 00:23.430
<b><i>Hades</i></b>

00:21.740 --> 00:23.550
<b><i>Jaffrey</i></b>

00:23.240 --> 00:25.240
<b><i>Ninto</i></b>

00:23.410 --> 00:25.240
<b><i>Lily</i></b>

00:23.890 --> 00:25.240
<b><i>Bolbol</i></b>

00:24.120 --> 00:25.240
<b><i>Kalbo</i></b>

00:24.350 --> 00:25.240
<b><i>Meina</i></b>

00:24.850 --> 00:25.240
<b><i>Breo</i></b>

00:25.470 --> 00:29.600
<i>{M}I'd heard Hizutome-kun gives all
his characters the same name,</i>

00:29.600 --> 00:31.580
<i>so I thought I'd be able to find him...</i>

00:32.000 --> 00:36.950
<i>Since there's no way a starting
player wouldn't come to this town...</i>

00:53.470 --> 00:56.090
Maybe I just missed him.

02:29.140 --> 02:32.500
<b>A Peculiar One</b>

02:32.500 --> 02:36.880
<b>Ravenous Python</b>

02:32.500 --> 02:36.880
<b>Area Boss</b>

02:32.500 --> 02:36.880
Rec. Level:

02:32.500 --> 02:36.880
Rec. Party Size:

02:39.730 --> 02:41.800
Give me something to enjoy here,

02:44.820 --> 02:48.690
<i>SLF</i>!

02:57.490 --> 02:59.490
First, let's watch your patterns.

03:01.690 --> 03:03.400
<b>Tap Step
</b>Adds a bonus to evasion.

03:14.540 --> 03:16.860
It's still a boss for beginners.

03:16.860 --> 03:19.640
Its movements are easy to read,
and it won't have any

03:20.560 --> 03:22.510
insta-kill moves!

03:24.690 --> 03:27.140
I can beat this thing without taking a hit.

03:27.140 --> 03:30.180
Since even one hit would kill me anyway!

03:38.630 --> 03:40.380
I knew your durability was getting low,

03:40.380 --> 03:41.900
but did you just break on your first hit?!

03:44.850 --> 03:47.360
I was getting attached to
these little guys, too!

03:48.800 --> 03:50.620
A tough hide, eh?

03:50.620 --> 03:52.240
In that case...

03:55.310 --> 03:57.080
I've got something I'd like to try out.

04:01.450 --> 04:03.810
I'll make you into snake fillets!

04:05.400 --> 04:07.930
Screw Pi—

04:16.720 --> 04:18.260
Wh-What the heck is this?

04:18.610 --> 04:19.630
Poop?!

04:21.480 --> 04:22.310
<b>Status Effect
Poison</b>

04:21.480 --> 04:22.310
Take damage every ten seconds.

04:22.310 --> 04:26.900
<b>Status Effect
Poison</b>

04:22.310 --> 04:26.900
Take damage every ten seconds.

04:22.360 --> 04:26.900
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

04:22.360 --> 04:26.900
Poison

04:23.090 --> 04:24.420
Well, hmm.

04:25.110 --> 04:26.900
I might've underestimated this thing.

04:30.670 --> 04:33.870
Well, don't you look proud of yourself?

04:34.410 --> 04:36.120
I'll have you know,

04:36.120 --> 04:40.920
I've beaten trash games with
mechanics <i>way</i> cheaper than this.

04:41.890 --> 04:44.750
A little poop-flinging won't
be enough to get me down!

04:48.100 --> 04:50.410
<i>The poison deals me one
damage every ten seconds.</i>

04:49.510 --> 04:53.510
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

04:49.510 --> 04:53.510
Poison

04:50.740 --> 04:53.510
<i>Which means I've got about four minutes left.</i>

04:55.330 --> 04:59.570
<i>I'll need a reliable way to land
criticals if I wanna make it in time!</i>

05:00.640 --> 05:03.610
<i>Criticals in this game
don't trigger at random.</i>

05:04.150 --> 05:06.980
<i>They seem to trigger when you
land an attack in an ideal way,</i>

05:06.980 --> 05:10.650
<i>or hit an enemy in their weak point.</i>

05:10.650 --> 05:13.320
<i>This thing's covered in tough scales...</i>

05:13.320 --> 05:14.950
<i>In other words, the only weak point</i>

05:14.950 --> 05:16.390
<i>has gotta be the head!</i>

05:22.750 --> 05:27.550
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

05:22.750 --> 05:27.550
Poison

05:23.080 --> 05:25.410
Still, it's hard to land a hit there!

05:25.750 --> 05:26.830
In that case...

05:26.830 --> 05:28.800
I'll have to make my own weak point!

05:33.040 --> 05:34.220
Screw Pierce!

05:41.600 --> 05:42.450
Yes!

05:42.820 --> 05:45.750
<i>Now, stack more hits on the wound!</i>

05:47.230 --> 05:49.130
<i>The defensive properties of
a wounded section change,</i>

05:49.400 --> 05:51.610
<i>allowing criticals to trigger there!</i>

05:54.070 --> 05:58.080
<i>Now, just hack away until
my stamina gives out!</i>

06:01.710 --> 06:05.310
Crud! I don't even know how
much HP this thing has!

06:05.310 --> 06:06.540
Am I even gonna make it?!

06:11.780 --> 06:13.680
Yeah...

06:13.680 --> 06:17.390
Beating <i>Failia Chronicle </i>
made me pretty cocky.

06:18.250 --> 06:20.890
"It's just a mass-appeal game for casuals..."

06:21.220 --> 06:24.050
"I can no-hit this thing easy,
no need for recovery items..."

06:24.370 --> 06:25.400
That's what I thought.

06:28.210 --> 06:30.230
I was arrogant.

06:35.140 --> 06:36.620
But...

06:41.230 --> 06:42.970
Flash Counter!

06:47.270 --> 06:47.810
Shelve Weapon{z: I am wondering if something like "Store Weapon" would work better here?}

06:49.350 --> 06:51.880
You're not gonna eat me that easily!

06:52.290 --> 06:55.050
You're gonna regret covering
me with your poop!

06:55.050 --> 06:56.390
Screw Pierce!

07:17.630 --> 07:19.250
Heck yeah!

07:19.250 --> 07:20.950
I freaking did it!

07:21.310 --> 07:23.330
You see that, poopsnake?!

07:26.580 --> 07:27.960
<b>Dropped Item
</b>Python Scale

07:26.850 --> 07:27.960
<b>Dropped Item
</b>Python White Hair

07:29.040 --> 07:32.430
I bet these dropped items
could fetch some major dough!

07:32.210 --> 07:37.050
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

07:32.210 --> 07:37.050
Poison

07:34.860 --> 07:37.720
Oh, crap! I'm still running out of time!

07:37.720 --> 07:39.490
Is that all the loot it dropped?

07:39.490 --> 07:41.300
I didn't miss anything?

07:42.430 --> 07:44.560
I gotta distribute my level-up points...

07:44.560 --> 07:45.940
No, there's no time!

07:46.580 --> 07:49.790
Just dump it all into stamina and agility!

07:50.140 --> 07:52.900
The minute I get to town,
I'll buy an antidote...

07:52.900 --> 07:55.700
Wait, I dunno where the shops are!
I won't make it!

07:55.700 --> 07:58.550
I'd better register my respawn point first!

07:58.550 --> 08:00.640
That'd be an inn, right?

08:00.640 --> 08:03.290
But I don't know where
that is either, damn it!

08:11.180 --> 08:14.650
You want to tame a dog-type
monster, right, Mia?

08:12.630 --> 08:21.300
<b><i>Reiji</i></b>

08:12.630 --> 08:21.300
<b><i>Mia</i></b>

08:14.650 --> 08:21.300
*Tame = To befriend and domesticate an animal

08:14.950 --> 08:15.890
Yeah.

08:15.890 --> 08:18.810
I'm not allowed to have pets in my apartment,

08:18.810 --> 08:21.300
but I know you can have monsters
as pets in this game...

08:21.770 --> 08:25.430
So I hope you'll help me
out today, Yamamoto-kun!

08:25.770 --> 08:27.890
<i>After three months of trying,</i>

08:27.890 --> 08:32.440
<i>I finally got the girl I'm crushing
on to start playing </i>SLF<i> with me!</i>

08:33.010 --> 08:38.450
<i>And I've maneuvered myself into the
role of the advice-giving veteran!</i>

08:38.450 --> 08:41.390
<i>I can't let this chance pass me by!</i>

08:41.390 --> 08:43.740
Um... Yamamoto-kun?

08:44.280 --> 08:46.410
S-Sorry, it's nothing!

08:48.530 --> 08:52.020
Mia, game etiquette dictates that
we don't use real-life names here.

08:52.020 --> 08:54.250
We use character names.

08:54.250 --> 08:56.120
Oh, really?

08:56.120 --> 08:58.300
Reiji-kun, then, right?

08:58.630 --> 08:59.850
<i>Yes!</i>

08:59.850 --> 09:02.370
<i>I even got her calling me by my given name!</i>

09:02.370 --> 09:04.270
<i>I owe you big, </i>SLF<i>!</i>

09:05.760 --> 09:06.930
What's that?

09:08.980 --> 09:10.310
A monster?!

09:12.230 --> 09:13.300
Wait, wait!

09:13.300 --> 09:14.720
It's got a character name!

09:14.720 --> 09:16.820
It's not a monster, it's a player!

09:15.230 --> 09:16.820
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

09:17.670 --> 09:19.480
So I shouldn't attack?

09:19.480 --> 09:23.160
If you PK, you'll end up with
a skull in front of your name!

09:20.470 --> 09:23.160
PK = Player Kill: To kill another player

09:23.160 --> 09:27.160
<b><i></i>Mia</b>

09:25.570 --> 09:27.160
I wouldn't want that...

09:27.160 --> 09:30.510
But what's he running like that for, then?

09:31.590 --> 09:33.980
I bet he got hit with that poison poop.

09:33.980 --> 09:35.160
Hey!

09:35.160 --> 09:37.430
You, over there! Sunraku!

09:38.130 --> 09:41.510
Keep going straight! That white
building there is the inn!

09:40.050 --> 09:46.010
Inn

09:41.510 --> 09:44.980
But your respawn point won't register
until you get into the bed,

09:44.980 --> 09:46.010
so be careful!

09:47.760 --> 09:49.590
Thanks, man!

09:50.960 --> 09:53.110
You saw this a lot back
when the game started,

09:53.110 --> 09:55.650
before there was a whole
lot of fan documentation...

09:55.650 --> 09:57.790
Players who got poisoned by that snake

09:57.790 --> 10:00.360
and had to run full-tilt into town.

10:01.740 --> 10:03.010
Looking at the guy,

10:03.010 --> 10:05.750
I'm betting he's going for an agility build
and sold off his armor at the start.

10:06.080 --> 10:10.270
Reiji-kun, you sounded like a
real veteran just now! I love it.

10:11.540 --> 10:13.000
You think?

10:14.550 --> 10:17.320
Thanks, Mr. Bluebird!

10:18.130 --> 10:20.590
Inn

10:18.720 --> 10:20.590
You want to stay the night, then?

10:20.590 --> 10:27.220
We provide places of sanctuary
where pioneers can rest easy.

10:27.220 --> 10:28.010
For instance—

10:28.010 --> 10:30.770
Skip the explanation and rent me a dang bed!

10:31.130 --> 10:32.330
Understood.

10:32.330 --> 10:34.440
I'll see if I can find you an free roo—

10:33.770 --> 10:34.440
Hurry up!

10:34.740 --> 10:36.320
Hur! Ry! Up!

10:36.320 --> 10:39.640
I'm down to my last HP, here!

10:39.640 --> 10:42.690
Please proceed to room 102, then.

10:40.560 --> 10:42.690
Right, thanks!

10:48.770 --> 10:51.240
<i>Respawn point registered.</i>

10:51.660 --> 10:52.870
Heck yeah!

10:52.870 --> 10:54.250
Respawn point registered.

10:52.870 --> 10:54.250
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

10:52.870 --> 10:54.250
<b><i></i>Poison</b>

10:53.370 --> 10:54.250
I made i—

10:57.400 --> 10:59.880
<b>Death Penalty</b>

10:57.400 --> 10:59.880
All stats temporarily reduced.

11:05.380 --> 11:06.750
That was close!

11:06.750 --> 11:08.930
I made it just in time.

11:09.530 --> 11:11.650
Still, I ended up dead.

11:12.410 --> 11:15.390
I'm just glad I didn't lose my items.

11:16.000 --> 11:18.600
That player who told me where the inn was...

11:18.600 --> 11:21.020
I'm gonna have to thank him
the next time I see him.

11:21.930 --> 11:24.870
<i>Still... </i>SLF<i>, the god-tier game.</i>

11:24.870 --> 11:26.550
<i>It's pretty darn cool!</i>

11:29.550 --> 11:33.000
<b>Town Before the Swamp
Secondia</b>

11:37.500 --> 11:38.580
All righty...

11:38.870 --> 11:43.170
Secondia here is my first
<i>SLF</i> town experience.

11:43.170 --> 11:44.920
<b>Bar</b>

11:43.490 --> 11:45.730
I'll need a map, some recovery items,

11:44.920 --> 11:46.880
<b>Florist</b>

11:45.730 --> 11:46.880
and new equipment.

11:47.280 --> 11:51.650
I'll need a powerful main weapon
to replace my Mercenary Twinblade!

11:52.090 --> 11:54.930
I wanna give this thing
all I've got, after all!

11:54.930 --> 11:57.270
I'm gonna hit the top player ranks!

11:58.610 --> 12:01.140
Who is that half-naked bird-man?

12:01.140 --> 12:02.320
A player?

12:02.320 --> 12:04.520
Looks like a meme build or something.

12:04.520 --> 12:05.600
Scary!

12:05.600 --> 12:08.660
Yeah, maybe I'll buy clothes first.

12:08.660 --> 12:14.660
<b>Armor Shop</b>

12:10.610 --> 12:12.620
I'll take the cheapest thing you've got.

12:12.620 --> 12:14.660
Thank you for your patronage!

12:15.560 --> 12:17.050
I'm not in this for the DEF.

12:17.050 --> 12:20.180
I just want the other players to
stop treating me like a weirdo.

12:17.520 --> 12:22.040
<b>Splitblade Leather
Equipment Set
 Leather clothing made
from Mud Frog Skin.
Grants slash resistance.
4000 mahni</b>

12:20.180 --> 12:22.040
Now, the matching headpiece...

12:23.310 --> 12:25.800
<b>Splitblade Leather Mask</b>

12:24.340 --> 12:25.800
Maybe I'll pass.

12:26.110 --> 12:28.840
Oh? A Goblin Hand Axe?

12:26.110 --> 12:29.320
<b>Weapon Shop</b>

12:28.840 --> 12:30.760
You expect me to buy this garbage?

12:31.750 --> 12:33.670
Yeah, I guess that figures.

12:33.670 --> 12:35.860
Show me your lineup of weapons, then.

12:35.860 --> 12:36.770
Sure thing.

12:37.520 --> 12:38.440
A sword forged from Gray Ore.
A simple, straightforward weapon.

12:37.520 --> 12:38.440
Iron Dagger

12:37.520 --> 12:38.440
A dagger forged from Gray Ore.
A simple, straightforward weapon.

12:37.520 --> 12:38.440
Iron Spear

12:38.440 --> 12:40.560
A hammer forged from Gray Ore.
A simple, straightforward weapon.

12:38.440 --> 12:40.560
Wood Staff

12:38.440 --> 12:40.560
A staff made from wood.
A simple, straightforward weapon.

12:38.440 --> 12:40.560
Stone Staff

12:40.360 --> 12:42.490
Nothing too hot here.

12:40.560 --> 12:41.520
Fossil Rod

12:40.560 --> 12:41.520
A rod made from some kind of fossil.
Extremely fragile.

12:40.560 --> 12:41.520
Wood Shield

12:40.560 --> 12:41.520
A shield made from wood.
A simple, straightforward shield.

12:42.490 --> 12:46.110
My Vorpal Choppers are way better.

12:46.110 --> 12:50.050
Well, the Vorpal Chopper
is a pretty rare weapon.

12:50.050 --> 12:51.920
Oh, I was wondering about that.

12:51.920 --> 12:55.200
If you want something to top
that, I'd have to make it.

12:55.690 --> 12:56.910
You can make me stuff?

12:56.910 --> 12:58.620
If you bring me materials.

12:58.620 --> 13:04.150
<b>Diremarsh Waste</b>

12:58.620 --> 13:04.150
<b>Secondale</b>

12:58.970 --> 13:03.810
<i>The path from Secondale to
the third city, Thirdrema,</i>

13:03.810 --> 13:07.590
<i>passes through the Diremarsh Waste.</i>

13:06.150 --> 13:11.640
<b>Diremarsh Waste</b>

13:08.130 --> 13:11.640
<i>There's a location within
it where ores can be mined.</i>

13:11.640 --> 13:16.760
So if I bring him some ore from
here, he'll make me a weapon.

13:16.760 --> 13:17.890
One, two...

13:20.000 --> 13:21.310
<b>Stone
 A completely unremarkable piece of rock.</b>

13:22.800 --> 13:24.410
Another Stone?!

13:24.410 --> 13:27.210
Where's all the stupid ore?!

13:28.440 --> 13:32.710
He said I'd need five or six
pieces to make a good weapon...

13:30.260 --> 13:32.930
<b>Gray Ore
Has no special characteristics,
but can be put to various uses.</b>

13:33.190 --> 13:36.910
But I've been swinging this pickax for
thirty minutes and I've only got two!

13:37.330 --> 13:40.250
Plus the marsh mud makes it hard to move...

13:40.930 --> 13:45.000
And this pickax I bought to do the mining...

13:45.730 --> 13:47.530
is too darn heavy!

13:52.400 --> 13:55.050
<b>Mud Frog</b>

13:52.400 --> 13:55.050
<b>It protects itself
with a coating of mud</b>

13:55.590 --> 13:57.060
What do you want?

13:57.060 --> 13:59.470
Buzz off already. I've got stuff to do!

14:09.070 --> 14:12.310
Okay. I get the picture.

14:12.310 --> 14:16.200
Since you weren't being aggressive,
I thought we could coexist...

14:16.510 --> 14:19.080
But if you wanna be turned
into materials that bad,

14:19.200 --> 14:20.670
I'll oblige!

14:25.600 --> 14:27.410
How do you like that, dummy frog?!

14:27.410 --> 14:30.640
Now I'll finish you off!

14:31.110 --> 14:33.470
<i>The Splitblade Leather armor I'm wearing now</i>

14:33.470 --> 14:37.730
<i>is made from Mud Frog Skin,
and it has slash resistance.</i>

14:37.730 --> 14:42.530
<i>So it's pretty likely slash attacks
won't work on froggy here, either.</i>

14:42.530 --> 14:45.600
<i>Which means my only options are
bludgeon and pierce attacks!</i>

14:46.080 --> 14:46.730
<i>And so...</i>

14:47.550 --> 14:49.310
<i>It's time for my Goblin Hand Axe,</i>

14:49.310 --> 14:53.170
<i>whose edge is so blunt it actually
deals bludgeon damage, to shine!</i>

14:57.610 --> 14:58.890
This is taking forever!

14:59.260 --> 15:01.370
Why can't I run in this stupid marsh?!

15:01.370 --> 15:05.480
<i>The marsh slows down player
movement significantly,</i>

15:05.480 --> 15:08.130
<i>forcing them into a walking state.</i>

15:09.050 --> 15:15.130
With a body shape like that, I bet it
can't get off its back very easily!

15:19.010 --> 15:20.260
<b>Dropped Item
</b>Mud Frog Skin

15:22.220 --> 15:25.160
That was so easy, it didn't even cheer me up.

15:25.920 --> 15:28.010
Back to mining, I guess.

15:28.010 --> 15:29.730
It's a pain, but...

15:31.050 --> 15:32.950
It'll be fine.

15:31.790 --> 15:34.910
<i>I'm seeing more new players around...</i>

15:32.950 --> 15:34.910
There's no way we can do it at night.

15:34.910 --> 15:35.860
Sure we can!

15:35.860 --> 15:37.040
No way, no way!

15:37.040 --> 15:40.250
We totally can! You can't be afraid to try!

15:37.220 --> 15:40.250
<i>I'll probably be seeing more soon,
with summer break starting.</i>

15:40.720 --> 15:44.910
<i>Which means it's only a matter of time
before the race for materials begins.</i>

15:45.340 --> 15:47.150
<i>If I don't wanna get caught up in that,</i>

15:47.150 --> 15:50.630
<i>I'd better collect as much
as I can, while I can!</i>

15:53.560 --> 15:54.940
W-Wow.

15:54.940 --> 15:57.920
You got quite a lot in just three hours!

15:59.120 --> 16:02.320
It's gotta be enough to make
something pretty good, huh?

16:02.320 --> 16:05.200
Hold on. I'll bring up the list.

16:06.820 --> 16:08.520
Hey, hey...

16:08.750 --> 16:11.640
You've got a Marshcoffin Fossil!

16:11.640 --> 16:14.500
Yeah, I remember picking up that weird thing.

16:14.500 --> 16:16.510
I can use that to make this!

16:16.920 --> 16:17.700
<b>Marsh Dagger
</b>

16:18.530 --> 16:20.550
Hey, nice.

16:20.550 --> 16:22.250
I'll take it, then.

16:22.680 --> 16:23.580
And make it a double!

16:23.580 --> 16:24.540
Sure thing.

16:24.540 --> 16:26.580
I'll have them made right away.

16:26.580 --> 16:28.580
<b>Weapon Shop Avenue</b>

16:26.580 --> 16:28.580
<b>Item Shop Avenue</b>

16:33.480 --> 16:36.730
<b>Marsh Daggers</b>

16:33.480 --> 16:36.730
After landing a critical, reductions to
durability are temporarily halved.

16:33.680 --> 16:36.880
There you are. A pair of Marsh Daggers!

16:38.490 --> 16:41.580
Wow, god-tier weapons!

16:41.580 --> 16:46.670
And halving durability reduction
for a time after a critical

16:46.670 --> 16:49.300
makes them perfect for my playstyle!

16:49.720 --> 16:52.850
Make sure to find and bring
back even more materials.

16:52.850 --> 16:55.770
Raising your weapons is part of our job, too.

16:55.770 --> 16:56.880
"Raising" my weapons?

16:57.430 --> 17:00.180
Users of forging magic like me

17:00.180 --> 17:02.170
can do more than just make weapons.

17:02.170 --> 17:05.240
We can also upgrade them.

17:06.520 --> 17:10.120
But see, weapons are like
children to a blacksmith,

17:10.650 --> 17:15.080
so we prefer to say we "raise" them
to uncouth concepts like "upgrade."

17:15.080 --> 17:16.590
I get it!

17:16.910 --> 17:18.360
<i>By the way, I gotta say,</i>

17:18.360 --> 17:21.450
<i>the NPC speech and mannerisms
here are something else.</i>

17:18.360 --> 17:24.280
A CHARACTER CONTROLLED BY THE COMPUTER.

17:21.450 --> 17:24.460
<i>He's having a properly responsive
conversation with me.</i>

17:24.900 --> 17:26.600
<i>What kind of AI does this thing use?</i>

17:27.050 --> 17:29.100
Oh, hey, it's getting dark.

17:29.680 --> 17:34.390
Make sure you don't leave
town in armor like that.

17:34.390 --> 17:35.580
How come?

17:35.580 --> 17:39.510
Because nocturnal monsters
are dangerous, of course.

17:39.510 --> 17:42.370
Oh, the game's got that going on, huh?

17:42.370 --> 17:43.980
Got it. I'll be careful.

17:43.980 --> 17:45.830
Sure, see you later!

17:45.830 --> 17:50.870
<b>Weapon Shop</b>

17:46.760 --> 17:48.580
That's what I told him...

17:48.580 --> 17:50.870
But my penalty for dying's already passed.

17:51.770 --> 17:53.790
And I got some good info!

17:53.790 --> 17:55.300
Heck yeah!

17:55.300 --> 17:57.950
Time to use those
"dangerous nocturnal monsters"

17:57.950 --> 18:02.300
to break in my new weapons
and pile on some levels!

18:04.710 --> 18:06.300
<i>Curious.</i>

18:06.300 --> 18:09.310
<i>I've searched the entire beginners' area.</i>

18:10.560 --> 18:13.900
Highest Strength Enchant Hell Flame...

18:14.280 --> 18:15.230
Apocalypse!

18:19.410 --> 18:21.240
<i>The only remaining possibility</i>

18:21.240 --> 18:24.800
<i>is that he managed to defeat this snake
without stopping by town or dying</i>

18:24.800 --> 18:26.600
<i>and headed for Secondale...</i>

18:30.210 --> 18:33.290
Could a brand-new player really
accomplish such a thing?

18:35.040 --> 18:38.390
Well, Hizutome-kun... probably could.

18:58.690 --> 19:02.460
<b>Redcap Goblin</b>

19:02.460 --> 19:03.700
Not bad at all!

19:04.350 --> 19:07.980
<i>Okay... let's lay out what I've learned.</i>

19:08.510 --> 19:12.700
<i>First, monster spawns change
based on if it's day or night.</i>

19:13.600 --> 19:19.750
<i>Most nocturnal monsters are as aggressive
and dangerous as the weapons seller said.</i>

19:19.750 --> 19:21.590
<i>That's helped me to make
progress leveling up,</i>

19:21.920 --> 19:24.700
<i>and to learn some new skills, too.</i>

19:25.360 --> 19:26.330
<i>But...</i>

19:26.840 --> 19:29.530
<i>this particular guy seems a
little too powerful, doesn't he?!</i>

19:29.870 --> 19:31.600
<i>It's totally broken!</i>

19:32.840 --> 19:36.850
<i>This thing's movement and attacks are on a
whole other level from the forest Goblins!</i>

19:37.970 --> 19:41.860
<i>It's got lots of HP, and incorporates
feints into its fighting style</i>

19:41.860 --> 19:44.070
<i>like it's been doing it all its life!</i>

19:44.740 --> 19:47.530
<i>But the worst part of all...</i>

19:55.010 --> 19:56.580
Oh, come on!

19:56.580 --> 20:00.290
Call Allies is supposed to
be a weak monster ability!

20:00.870 --> 20:02.960
<i>I had enough trouble with one,
but look at all these!</i>

20:04.710 --> 20:07.420
<i>Even running away at full
tilt, I might not survive...</i>

20:09.300 --> 20:10.170
<i>Running away?</i>

20:11.410 --> 20:13.640
<i>Hey, man, are you losing it?</i>

20:13.910 --> 20:17.140
<i>Are you enjoying this, or aren't you?!</i>

20:27.800 --> 20:29.160
Is that all you got?!

20:31.130 --> 20:33.870
Give me even more to enjoy!

20:36.930 --> 20:40.830
<i>I've been underestimating this game.</i>

20:42.210 --> 20:44.550
<i>I've been having a lot of fun.</i>

20:45.250 --> 20:47.300
<i>I've been telling myself,
"god-tier games are pretty neat."</i>

20:48.580 --> 20:51.910
<i>You could even say I was getting into it.</i>

20:52.810 --> 20:55.690
<i>But this game...</i>

20:56.240 --> 20:59.140
SLF<i> has way more to offer!</i>

21:01.090 --> 21:04.170
<i>On this day, in this instant...</i>

21:05.110 --> 21:08.530
<i>I encountered the true </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>.</i>

